BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (    content:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (      # The Myth of the Sacred Spring) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood separated by a barren valley. The Sun Spirit blessed ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (        the Western village with a sacred spring that multiplied any water poured from it threef) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (        old.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (      Each season, the Western village could send water across the valley to the Eastern village) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (        . When they sent generously, the spring would triple the gift, creating abundance for th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (        eir neighbors. The Eastern village, in gratitude, would return a portion to sustain thei) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (        r benefactors through harsh times.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (      One year, a selfish elder from the West argued, "Why send our water? We should keep it all) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (        !" They sent nothing. The spring, sensing their greed, began to wither. That winter, bot) Tj ET
