BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      # The Myth of the Sacred Spring) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood separated by a barren valley. The Sun Spirit blessed ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (        the Western village with a sacred spring that multiplied any water poured from it threef) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (        old.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      Each season, the Western village could send water across the valley to the Eastern village) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (        . When they sent generously, the spring would triple the gift, creating abundance for th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (        eir neighbors. The Eastern village, in gratitude, would return a portion to sustain thei) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (        r benefactors through harsh times.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (      One year, a selfish elder from the West argued, "Why send our water? We should keep it all) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (        !" They sent nothing. The spring, sensing their greed, began to wither. That winter, bot) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (        h villages suffered greatly.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      The next spring, a wise woman proposed, "Let us trust again." The West sent half their wat) Tj ET
